BANGALORE DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY
PUBLIC NOTICE NO. BDA/ZR/2024/150/0892

NOTICE UNDER SECTION 14 & 15 OF THE KARNATAKA TOWN AND COUNTRY PLANNING ACT, 1961
AND UNDER THE GREATER BANGALORE GOVERNANCE ACT, 2024

Sub: Revision of Commercial Setback Regulations and Land Use Reclassification - Ward 150 (Bellandur, Bengaluru)

Ref: BDA Master Plan 2031, Clause 7.3 and 9.1; BBMP Zoning Regulation Amendment G.O. No. UDD/232/2024

------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 1: BACKGROUND AND AUTHORITY
------------------------------------------------------------------
The Bangalore Development Authority (BDA), exercising its statutory powers under Section 14 of the Karnataka Town and Country Planning Act, 1961 (KTCP Act) and the Greater Bangalore Governance Act, 2024 (GBGA 2024), hereby issues this public notice for proposed amendments to the Zoning Regulations applicable to Ward 150 (Bellandur Zone, Outer Ring Road Corridor).

This notice supersedes previous zoning circular BDA/ZR/2022/150/0341 dated 14-March-2022.

------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 2: PROPOSED ZONING AMENDMENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 COMMERCIAL SETBACK REVISION
Effective from the date of gazette notification (anticipated Q2 2024), all commercial buildings on plots measuring between 1000 sq ft and 5000 sq ft within Ward 150 shall maintain a mandatory front setback of 3.0 metres from the plot boundary. This revision increases the current mandatory setback of 1.8 metres by 1.2 metres under BDA Regulation Clause 9.1(b).

Impact: All existing commercial establishments on plots between 1000-5000 sq ft that do not currently comply with the 3.0m setback requirement will be deemed non-conforming structures under Section 12 of the KTCP Act, 1961.

2.2 LAND USE RECLASSIFICATION - FROM MIXED RESIDENTIAL TO COMMERCIAL ZONE
Survey numbers 42, 43, 44, 67, and 68 of Bellandur Village, Ward 150, are hereby proposed for reclassification from Mixed Residential (MR-2) to Commercial (C-2) zone. This reclassification allows for higher-intensity commercial development as per BDA Master Plan 2031, Clause 7.3.

Estimated affected area: 12.4 acres.
Estimated affected households: 340 residential units currently occupying survey numbers 42-68.

2.3 PROPERTY TAX REVISION UNDER SECTION 108A
Pursuant to the reclassification in 2.2, properties within the reclassified C-2 zone shall attract revised Annual Rental Value (ARV) computation under BBMP Property Tax Regulation, Section 108A. Commercial ARV rates (Rs. 18-45 per sq ft per annum) shall replace existing residential ARV rates (Rs. 4-8 per sq ft per annum), resulting in an estimated 3x to 5x increase in annual property tax liability for affected property owners.

------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 3: IMPACT ON SMALL COMMERCIAL ESTABLISHMENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------
The revised 3.0m setback regulation will disproportionately impact small commercial establishments (SCE) operating on plots below 2000 sq ft. The BDA Technical Committee (TC/2024/89) noted that approximately 68% of SCEs in Ward 150 operate on plots between 1000-2000 sq ft and currently maintain setbacks of only 0.9m to 1.5m. Compliance with the revised setback would require demolition or significant structural modification to front-facing structures.

Shop tenants in Ward 150 (estimated 1,200 active commercial tenants) may face operational disruption during mandatory compliance retrofitting. No displacement compensation framework has been proposed in this notice.

------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 4: OBJECTION PERIOD AND PUBLIC CONSULTATION
------------------------------------------------------------------
Citizens, property owners, and commercial establishments affected by this notice are entitled to file written objections under Section 15(3) of the KTCP Act, 1961. All objections must be submitted to:

The Joint Commissioner (Zoning),
Bangalore Development Authority,
Kumara Park East, Bengaluru - 560 001.

OBJECTION DEADLINE: 30 days from the date of publication of this notice in the Karnataka Gazette.

A public hearing will be conducted at the BDA Head Office on the date to be notified separately in the Official Gazette.

------------------------------------------------------------------
